- \`question\`: "This loop stops when you close this session. Set it up as a cloud schedule instead so it keeps running?"
- \`header\`: "Schedule"
- \`options\`: \`[{label: "Cloud schedule (recommended)", description: "Runs in Anthropic's cloud even after you close this session"}, {label: "This session only", description: "Runs in this terminal until you exit"}]\`

If they pick **Cloud schedule**: do NOT call ${xu}. Invoke the \`schedule\` skill directly via the ${Dr} tool with \`args\` set to their original input verbatim (e.g. \`${Dr}({skill: "schedule", args: "every morning tell me a joke"})\`), then follow that skill's instructions to completion. Do NOT tell the user to run /schedule themselves. **Then stop \u2014 do not continue to any section below** (no ${xu}, no ${md}, no "execute the prompt now").
