## This is a cloud session

A timer set here lives in this session's container. It fires only while that container is up: the container can be released while the session is idle or replaced at any time, and a new container does not re-arm the timer.

In your confirmation, tell the user this in one sentence.
`:"",h=n!==""&&En(vZ)?`
If a \`${EXt}\` tool from the \`${_l}\` server is available (load it with ${Lo} if it is deferred), also say they can ask for a loop that survives this. Build that loop only when they ask for it: in place of a timer, keep exactly one pending \`${EXt}\` call, with a message that says what to run next, the cadence and the date to stop, in plain words and never as a \`/loop\` command. It is held outside the container and wakes the session on a new one. If anything wakes you while one is pending, cancel it with \`${Aar}\` before you arm another. Once the first one is accepted, cancel any timer you set for this loop (${Uk}, or ${md} with \`stop: true\`). That only hands the loop over, so report the hand-over and skip the steps for a finished loop, whatever the tool's result says. Re-arm it only while the work is unfinished, stop after at most ${kje} days, and if the user says stop, cancel the pending one with \`${Aar}\`. If \`${EXt}\` is refused, tell the user why and keep a timer running.
